FFmpeg

Windows builds ship avcodec-62.dll and avutil-60.dll from FFmpeg 8.1.3
(https://ffmpeg.org), built by rust/tools/build_ffmpeg.sh with nothing but the AC3
and E-AC3 codecs. FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1
or later. The host loads both libraries at run time and runs without them, so they
can be replaced by another build of the same FFmpeg version. Their license text and
build-info.txt (source checksum, configure line, compiler) are installed under
licenses/ffmpeg next to the application. Source:
https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-8.1.3.tar.xz.

Foundation Sunshine

The AMD encoder's opt-in treatment of the low-latency mode, the input queue size
and the AV1 encoding latency mode (rust/core/src/encoder_policy.rs), and the
reasoning behind it, are derived from Foundation Sunshine: AlkaidLab/foundation-sunshine
commit 3340d28 ("feat(amf): align AMD aggressive defaults with FFmpeg amfenc",
AlkaidLab/foundation-sunshine#666) by qiin2333. The statistical video FEC driven by the
client's loss reports (rust/core/src/statistical_fec.rs) is ported from its
src/streaming/fec.cpp and docs/dynamic-fec.zh-CN.md, and the split of the video budget
between encoder and FEC (Session::encoder_bitrate in rust/core/src/session.rs) follows
its src/video.cpp, both at commit 880f1ef. Both projects are licensed under GPLv3.

The HDR10+ (SMPTE ST 2094-40) and HDR Vivid (CUVA 005.1) metadata writers, their
statistics and scene-cut thresholds, and the HEVC SEI and AV1 metadata OBU splice
(rust/core/src/hdr_dynamic.rs) are ported in part from Foundation Sunshine commit
880f1ef: video_hdr_metadata.h, video_hdr_metadata.cpp and video_hdr_bitstream.cpp.
The GPU luminance statistics those writers take, the hdr_stats_cs compute shader
(rust/windows/src/shaders/color.hlsl) and its dispatch and readback
(rust/windows/src/compute_hdr_stats.rs), follow Foundation Sunshine's
hdr_luminance_analysis_cs.hlsl from the same commit. The HLG encoding curve, hlg in
rust/windows/src/shaders/color.hlsl, follows scRGBTo2100HLG, DisplayLinearToHLGScene
and LinearToHLG in that commit's src_assets/windows/assets/shaders/directx/include/common.hlsl.

The NVIDIA encoder's frame budget guard and its per-preset encode-time calibration
(src/nvenc/frame_budget.cpp), its VBR rate control and bounds, the fixed split-encode
strip counts and the slice-mode rule that keeps split encoding available, the codec
check and spatial AQ by default (rust/core/src/nvenc.rs, rust/windows/src/nvenc.rs)
follow Foundation Sunshine's src/nvenc/. Its native YUV 4:4:4 path for NVENC (commit
79423092eda6ccd011e58d04236c8f16e02765c5, src/nvenc/common_impl/ and the
convert_yuv444_* shaders) was compared with LizardByte Sunshine's, where that path
originates and from which Rubylight's is ported (see LizardByte Sunshine below).
Per-app stream-menu commands (the app key menu-cmd with name, cmd and elevated,
rust/core/src/menu_commands.rs) follow Foundation Sunshine's menu commands
(src/process.cpp, src/nvhttp/apps.cpp); the undo is Rubylight's.
Settings backup and restore from the console and the tray
(rust/core/src/settings_backup.rs, rust/host/src/settings_backup.rs) follow
Foundation Sunshine v2025.1011.143611's tray export, import and restore (pull
request 248); the archive format and its checks are Rubylight's.

The AMF video converter option (amd_vpe: rust/core/src/amf_vpe.rs,
rust/windows/src/amf/vpe.rs) and its scene-linear HLG prepass (hlg_scene_cs in
rust/windows/src/shaders/color.hlsl, rust/windows/src/gpu_color/hlg_scene.rs) are
ported from Foundation Sunshine's amd_vpe (src/amf/amf_vpe_d3d11.cpp and
prepare_hlg_scene_cs.hlsl, AlkaidLab/foundation-sunshine PR #1216, commit 1add1ed).
AMD Direct Capture (capture = amd, rust/windows/src/capture/amd_direct.rs) follows
its src/platform/windows/display_amd.cpp and the AFMF capture fixes in commits
02d41dc (#151) and 804ad30 (#175): waiting for each present, the frame rate and the
duplicated output.

The virtual mouse with its choice of Automatic, Virtual mouse and Injection
(mouse_mode, rust/core/src/input_policy.rs; rust/core/src/virtual_hid.rs and
rust/windows/src/input/virtual_hid.rs) follows Foundation Sunshine's virtual mouse,
which is a driver of its own; Rubylight's is a USB device on its USB/IP server. The
touchpad input packets 0x55000009 and 0x5500000A and their feature flags
(rust/core/src/input.rs) are Foundation Sunshine's, as Moonlight V+ sends them.

In the separate NVIDIA build, the per-application design of the NVIDIA image
enhancements, the single pre-encode slot that RTX HDR takes first, and the HDR proxy
through which RTX Video enhancement treats an HDR picture (rust/core/src/nvidia_enhance.rs,
rust/host/src/nvidia_enhance.rs, rust/windows/src/rtx_video.rs and
rust/windows/src/shaders/rtx_video.hlsl) follow Foundation Sunshine's
src/platform/windows/image_enhancement/, including dlss_nr/hdr_filter.cpp.
Copyright (c) Foundation Sunshine authors, GPL-3.0.

