LizardByte Sunshine

The NVIDIA encoder's native YUV 4:4:4 path is ported from LizardByte Sunshine
(https://github.com/LizardByte/Sunshine) commit
ec2676b60bb8220a1807fc761bc2157e5e6dba63: the input formats, 8-bit AYUV written
through an R8G8B8A8_UINT view and 10-bit as three R16_UINT planes stacked in one
texture and copied through CUDA (src/nvenc/nvenc_utils.cpp, nvenc_d3d11_native.cpp,
nvenc_d3d11_on_cuda.cpp, src/platform/windows/display_vram.cpp; rust/core/src/nvenc.rs,
rust/windows/src/gpu_color.rs), the conversion shaders' output layout
(src_assets/windows/assets/shaders/directx/include/convert_yuv444_ps_base.hlsl and
convert_yuv444_planar_vs.hlsl; yuv444_* in rust/windows/src/shaders/color.hlsl), and
the YUV 4:4:4 capability check (validate_encoder_capabilities in src/nvenc/nvenc_base.cpp;
rust/windows/src/nvenc.rs). The dscp_tagging switch, on by default, that turns off the
DSCP marks on video and audio (rust/core/src/stream_policy.rs) follows LizardByte
Sunshine pull request 6067. Copyright (c) LizardByte and the Sunshine contributors, GPL-3.0.

The Dolby Vision profile 8.1 RPU writer (rust/core/src/dovi.rs) follows the syntax,
default values and L1 limits of the dolby_vision crate 3.4.0 of dovi_tool
(https://github.com/quietvoid/dovi_tool, tag libdovi-3.4.0), Copyright (c) 2026
quietvoid, MIT. The MIT terms are included in rust/THIRD_PARTY.md.

